/-! # Off-rank vanishing of pulled-back Koszul Ext stalks

Source: Stacks Project, Tag 0BQZ. -/

@[expose] public section

universe u w

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits Opposite

namespace AlgebraicGeometry

/-- The pulled-back scalar Ext stalk vanishes when its degree differs from conormal rank.

Source: Stacks Project, Tag 0BQZ, proof of lemma-regular-immersion-ext.
(blueprint: lem-sc-koszul-ext-off-rank-stalk).

Proof: Choose at z an affine chart on which the ideal is generated by a finite
Koszul-regular sequence of length m. Its augmentation is a bounded finite free
resolution of the quotient. Restriction of derived internal Hom and the finite
free Hom model identify the restriction of scalar Ext with the sheafified
cohomology of the dual Koszul complex extended to integer degrees. The dual
Koszul cohomology theorem makes this zero away from degree m, including negative
degrees. The regular conormal basis and affine conormal frame compute the
conormal stalk finrank as m; hr identifies m with r(z). Thus hq puts the degree
outside m. Pullback after cohomology preserves the local zero sheaf, so its
stalk at z is zero. This argument neither pulls back a resolution nor uses
derived base change. The empty sequence is covered by the degree-zero Koszul
calculation; an empty Z has no z to check. No Noetherian hypothesis is needed.
Transporting through the common K-injective Hom complex handles the supplied
derived universe without a universe restriction on the conclusion. -/
theorem koszulRegularImmersion_ext_offRank_stalk
    {Z Y : Scheme.{u}} (i : Z ⟶ Y) [IsClosedImmersion i]
    [HasDerivedCategory.{w} (SheafOfModules.{u} (moduleRings Y.toRingedSpace))]
    (hregular : ∀ z : Z, ∃ U : Y.affineOpens, i z ∈ U.1 ∧
      ∃ (n : ℕ) (f : Fin n → Γ(Y, U.1)),
        Ideal.span (Set.range f) = i.ker.ideal U ∧
          RingTheory.Sequence.IsKoszulRegular f)
    (r : LocallyConstant Z ℕ)
    (hr : ∀ z : Z, r z = Module.finrank (Z.presheaf.stalk z)
      ((RingedSpace.moduleStalkFunctor Z.toRingedSpace z).obj
        ((Scheme.Modules.tensorPullback i).obj i.ker.toModules)))
    (q : ℤ) (z : Z) (hq : q ≠ (r z : ℤ)) :
    let F : Y.Modules := (DerivedCategory.homologyFunctor
      (SheafOfModules.{u} (moduleRings Y.toRingedSpace)) q).obj
        ((derivedInternalHom (Opens.grothendieckTopology Y) Y.toRingedSpace.sheaf).obj
          (op ((DerivedCategory.singleFunctor
            (SheafOfModules.{u} (moduleRings Y.toRingedSpace)) 0).obj
              ((Scheme.Modules.pushforward i).obj (SheafOfModules.unit Z.ringCatSheaf))),
            (DerivedCategory.singleFunctor
              (SheafOfModules.{u} (moduleRings Y.toRingedSpace)) 0).obj
                (SheafOfModules.unit Y.ringCatSheaf)))
    IsZero ((RingedSpace.moduleStalkFunctor Z.toRingedSpace z).obj
      ((Scheme.Modules.tensorPullback i).obj F)) := by sorry

end AlgebraicGeometry
